   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "wegen, trotz and während",
     "texto": [
      "**Wegen des Regens** (because of the rain) and **trotz des Regens** (despite the rain) take the genitive. **Während des Sommers** (during the summer) too.",
      "In everyday speech «wegen» is used a lot with the dative: **wegen dem Regen**; in an exam, the genitive is better."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "während as a conjunction",
     "texto": [
      "**Während** also means \"while\" (conjunction) and takes a clause: **Während ich arbeite, höre ich Musik** (lesson 21). With a noun it is a preposition and takes the genitive. Watch out for the false friend: **trotz** doesn't mean \"piece\"; it means \"despite\"."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
